Subject: corelib: include what you use, for headers wasi-libc does not pull in

WHAT / WHY

  src/corelib/global/qsimd.cpp
      qDetectCpuFeatures() calls getenv("QT_NO_CPU_FEATURE") with a comment
      saying "Intentionally NOT qgetenv (this code runs too early)", but the
      file includes only <stdio.h>, <string.h> and <assert.h>. glibc's and
      Apple's <stdio.h> drag in enough to declare getenv anyway; wasi-libc's
      does not, so the call is a hard "use of undeclared identifier 'getenv'"
      (helpfully mis-suggested by clang as 'qgetenv', which then compounds into
      "calling 'qgetenv' with incomplete return type 'QByteArray'").
      Adding <stdlib.h> is the whole fix.

UPSTREAM
  yes. A plain include-what-you-use defect that happens to be invisible on the
  platforms Qt currently builds on. Nothing wasi-specific in the hunk, so it is
  applied unconditionally rather than under Q_OS_WASI.

---
diff --git a/src/corelib/global/qsimd.cpp b/src/corelib/global/qsimd.cpp
index e60c828..aee4049 100644
--- a/src/corelib/global/qsimd.cpp
+++ b/src/corelib/global/qsimd.cpp
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include "qalgorithms.h"
 
 #include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>     // getenv() -- see qDetectCpuFeatures() below
 #include <string.h>
 
 #if defined(QT_NO_DEBUG) && !defined(NDEBUG)
